{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'func Test' pose-mcp/internal/pose/*index*test.go | rg 'Governance|Binding|Consumed|Current'; rg -n 'func projectRoot|func resolveGitChangeSet' pose-mcp/internal/cli/*.go; sed -n '165,240p' .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md; rg -n 'source|checkIndexInputs|indexInputBinding' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view*test.go | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_index_test.go:55:func TestGovernanceReadViewIndexConsumptionChecksBoundInputsOnlyWhenUsed(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_inputs_test.go:21:func TestModuleDiscoveryBindingTracksNestedManifestNamesOnly(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_inputs_test.go:53:func TestValidationResultsBindingTracksOutcome(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_inputs_test.go:70:func TestSmokeResultsBindingTracksSourceInventoryWithoutIndexRead(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_inputs_test.go:83:func TestReleaseStatusBindingTracksTagMovement(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation_test.go:101:func TestIndexGenerationBlockedOutputNeverLeavesAMixedCurrentSet(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation_test.go:324:func TestIndexGenerationDivergentInputBindingIsStaleNotUnavailable(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go:429:func projectRoot() (string, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go:437:func projectRootAt(dir string) (string, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:196:func resolveGitChangeSet(root, spec, base, head string) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:200:func resolveGitChangeSetIn(files posemodel.Files, root, spec, base, head string) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:204:func resolveGitChangeSetWithFiles(files posemodel.Files, root, spec, base, head string) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:226:func resolveGitChangeSetWithTrailers(root, spec, base, head string, captured []string) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:230:func resolveGitChangeSetWithTrailersIn(files posemodel.Files, root, spec, base, head string, captured []string) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:256:func resolveGitChangeSetWithTrailersAndFiles(files posemodel.Files, root, spec, base, head string, captured []string) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:263:func resolveGitChangeSetWithPatchDigest(files posemodel.Files, root, spec, base, head string, captured []string, patchDigest []byte) (posemodel.ChangeSet, error) {\nThe engine does not promise an atomic filesystem snapshot, detect an external\nABA that leaves identical final bytes, or defend against writers that bypass\nPOSE fencing. Such inputs cannot authorize an effect whose contract requires\ntransition evidence. More producers become current only when their read paths,\ncoverage and writer boundaries are explicitly brought under the view.\n\n\n## Accepted amendment — 2026-11-06: bounded multi-scope coordination (D7)\n\nThe real global strict check exhausted the shared governance record/metadata\nbudget across independent historical closeout evaluations. Separate the global\ncoordinator from scope operations: capture policy, candidate enumeration and the\nbounded immutable catalogue under an explicitly bound coordinator; audit those\nselection inputs after all workers join, including disabled-policy and empty\ncandidate paths. Each scope, recursive children and exactly authorized federated\nroots use their own bounded capture and final audit. Bound worker concurrency\nand retain evaluated results, not every scope's captured closure.\n\nCatalogue reuse must expose an explicit binding-aware interface; do not bypass\nroot, project, resolver or Files identity checks by unwrapping a live view. Buffer\nfindings until the relevant scope and coordinator audits complete. A localized\nloss must remain unknown and make the global gate fail without exhausting an\nunrelated sibling. Preserve complete historical review and attestation reads,\nlater negative decisions, replacements, child validity and current trust checks.\n\nThis composes coherent global selection and individually audited scope results.\nIt does not certify one simultaneous filesystem snapshot across every scope.\nThe existing per-operation caps remain unchanged. Keep real domain errors with\nclosure audit errors; unavailable metadata and exhausted budgets are not proof\nof an escaping path or observed content mutation. Regression tests must exercise\nthe real global orchestration under injected small budgets and serial/parallel\nworkers, selection interleavings, localized exhaustion, retention negatives and\nexact binding checks. Native whole-corpus verification is still required.\n\n\n## Instance execution configuration boundary (D8) — 2026-11-06\n\nThe user-authorized native review uses a local delegation policy with concrete\nvendors, executables, access and executor issuer. Keep that live policy out of the\nembedded scaffold through the existing instance-policy exclusion mechanism.\nThe target instance uses its native delegation setup and its own configuration;\nno engine-local agent profile or issuer becomes a target default. This preserves\nthe same authority boundary as neutral review policy and changes no capability\nadoption, historical record or review verdict.\n\n\n## Bounded executable identity for the selected review agent (D9) — 2026-11-06\n\nThe installed native Claude Code 2.1.318 executable is 337,814,032 bytes. Its\nprovenance setup failed before the vendor ran because executable hashing reused\nthe 256 MiB transcript-retention bound. Hash executables as a stream bounded to\n512 MiB, separately from evidence retention. Keep regular-file and identity\nchecks, bounded reads and rejection above that limit. Keep transcript and B34\nread-view budgets unchanged. Do not substitute a launcher to evade the selected\nexecutable's identity proof. This accepts the measured distribution with bounded\nheadroom; larger future distributions still require an explicit reassessment.\n\n\n### Provider framing for the instance-owned review profile\n\nClaude's stream repeats session_id in init and result events. The instance\nprofile selects the unique system/init event so the existing ambiguity guard\nand private-session redaction remain intact. A restricted, noninteractive review\nuses Read/Grep/Glob/Bash without Edit/Write/Agent tools or plan approval mode.\nThis changes neither independence nor stream/output/run limits; the actual\nworking tree remains checked for mutation. No vendor profile becomes a scaffold\ndefault.\n\n\n## Capacity recalibration of captured input bytes (D10) — 2026-11-13\n\nClosing spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, `pose index` in a\nfresh clone and then in the maintainer checkout refused the pose-dist corpus:\n`index.delivery-integrity` exceeded the captured-input budget and\n`index.generate` was left without a complete observation. Measured with a Git\nshim on the real builder: the change sets of every spec read `git show\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_index_test.go:93:\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"a consumed index with stale source bindings left its consumer current\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:14:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\".pose/project.json\": `{\"schema_version\":1,\"project_id\":\"proj.001\",\"name\":\"git view fixture\"}`, \"source.go\": \"package source\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:22:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"source revision was not captured: output=%q binding=%q\", first, view.operation.roots[0].revision)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:24:\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \"source.go\"), []byte(\"package source\\nfunc Changed() {}\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:27:\tsnapshotTestGit(t, root, \"add\", \"source.go\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:43:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.go\": \"package source\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:59:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.go\": \"package source\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:79:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.go\": \"package source\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git_test.go:152:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.go\": \"package source\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:15:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.txt\": \"version A\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:16:\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \"source.txt\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:40:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.txt\": \"version A\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:41:\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \"source.txt\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:71:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"index build requiring a source revision did not report unknown coverage: %v\", err)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:76:\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.txt\": \"physical\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:77:\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \"source.txt\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:142:\t\t\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"source.txt\": \"version A\\n\"})\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_capture_test.go:143:\t\t\tpath := filepath.Join(root, \"source.txt\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
