{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo defects found. The delegation preserves binding checks, shares computation through the coordinator’s synchronized memo, and leaves other scope reads independently audited.\n\nFocused race tests and additional index/registry tests passed. The exact-range artifact check found no errors; surface-check reported zero findings. Full validation uses the sealed pipeline evidence. The reported 2.5 GB corpus measurement was not independently reproduced.\n\nApplied pose-review, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Repository unchanged; no attestation recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified exact Store binding checks, authorized-root-vector comparison, synchronized memo publication, and production worker joining before coordinator audit. Scope callbacks must finish their workers before returning; check.go satisfies this lifecycle contract. The corpus memory measurement remains reported evidence rather than an independently reproduced benchmark. Atomic snapshots and external ABA detection remain outside the existing contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently ran the focused integration selection with -race: passed. Delegation pointers are initialized before callback execution; existing mutex and ready-channel synchronization publishes the shared result safely. Production workers join before the coordinator audit. No new asynchronous lifecycle or cancellation contract is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change adds internal operation fields and delegation only. CLI, MCP, persisted schemas, and public signatures remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing missing-binding, stale-binding, root-resolution, bounded-read, and audit errors remain in the path. Returned shared reasons are copied and applied to each consuming scope. Focused binding-refusal and exhaustion tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected production composition in check.go: scope results remain buffered until the coordinator returns, and coordinator audit errors prevent a green gate. Federated binding computation uses the coordinator resolver and authorized root routing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Shared checks retain input-specific reasons; coordinator failures preserve changed/unknown typed causes and bounded path context. No new logging or sensitive output is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the complete implementation diff and existing callers. Public CLI, file, and MCP contracts are unchanged. Historical approval, later rejection, retired binding, and independent closure tests continue to pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused race tests passed, proving one computation per input across concurrent scopes and coordinator rejection of changed shared inputs. Additional index-consumption, roadmap-child, and registry-final-audit tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 addresses duplicated computation and retained reads by delegating only index-input checks to the existing coordinator memo. R2 keeps those reads under its final audit. review_operation_view.go:648 preserves root-vector authorization before delegation at line 656; governance_read_view.go:644 delegates through coordinator Files. Production composition waits for scopes and propagates coordinator audit errors.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-e0fdbb6a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR D12 amendment records D1's choice to reuse the coordinator closure instead of introducing a process-wide material cache, implementing R1 and R2 while preserving independent scope captures.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared ADR D12, spec R1/R2, implementation comments, and validation-matrix selection. They consistently describe coordinator-owned checks, coordinator final auditing, unchanged scope captures, and no simultaneous snapshot guarantee.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined error propagation through scope and coordinator wrappers into check.go. Input changes, unavailable bindings, and budget exhaustion remain actionable failures with input/path context; callback and audit causes remain joined.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is covered by the concurrent computation-count test and R2 by the changed-input coordinator-audit test; both passed independently under -race. The spec records the configured 16-worker corpus run completing at 2.5 GB, below its 4 GB target; that benchmark was not independently repeated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the sealed range with the five declared artifacts. Implementation is confined to coordinator delegation and a test observation hook; regression tests, matrix registration, and ADR amendment support R1/R2. Generated governance artifacts do not expand runtime scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified scopeCatalogue still enforces root, project, resolver, Files identity, and active lifecycle before delegation. Authorized root vectors must match. Shared reads use captured coordinator Files and bounded routing; no new authority, credentials, dependencies, or external execution is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared delegation with D1's process-cache alternative. Reusing the existing operation memo and final audit is the smallest sufficient change and avoids inventing a complete process-cache invalidation key. It adds no speculative public abstraction. The choice would need reassessment if scopes acquired different authorized bindings or results were published before coordinator audit.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-check-shares-the-federated-material --strict --from 729501a0b91a4ff6ca5c0aebc46eb0b82ba10128 --to 3ab01deb38df5edf8aa073c9c0302b9607ef91a0 --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the required default command, then explicitly constrained the range because default trailer resolution included a commit beyond the sealed head. Exact-range reconciliation matched all five claims and returned no non-warning findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used sealed structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6 and independently inspected the spec, ADR, implementation, and production composition. Avoided assessment writes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Component discovery adds no necessary evidence for this internal delegation change. Inspected component code and sealed validation evidence without refreshing assessment artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No public API, event, Protobuf, or MCP contract changed. Independently inspected coordinator/scope and federated-root boundaries and used sealed integration evidence without assessment writes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Manually inspected the complete implementation diff and searched changed code for TODO, FIXME, stub, and panic markers; none were introduced. Avoided assessment writes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the completed review attestation. This independent review does not record attestations or perform closeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the completed review attestation; POSE must run it after recording this conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules and consulted the review workflow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-check-shares-the-federated-material --strict: one target, 226 results, zero findings. Inspected production reachability through check.go.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposed from the sealed strict pipeline run and inspected delivery-validation.json: 226 executed, 226 passed, zero failures or errors. Did not rerun the environment-dependent full pipeline.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed strict validation covering pose-mcp build, unit, integration, and e2e checks. Independently reran the focused integration selection with -race and additional index/registry tests; all passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
